Z||000000||DreXteR||04-17-2001||03:21 PM||||A VSS from a 5speed can be used in a 4speed??<P><BR>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierohoho||04-22-2001||12:36 PM||||Doesn't look like too many people know about these but I'll give it a try. They should interchange fine but the nylon gears which push on may be a different diameters. Pay close attention to that. The size difference is obvious and I think they may even be different colors. My '85 coupe had no working speedo when I got it due to a shop doing the clutch (5-speeed) and somewhere along the way swaping the VSS. I took another VSS out of a Pontiac with an auto and swapped gears and it worked fine. Don't put 12V to the sending wires like they did to trace the problem, that was a mess to fix. E-me if you have any questions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||04-22-2001||05:05 PM||||5 spds use a BLUE gear<BR>4 spds use a RED ger<P><BR> however the VSS unit is INTERCHANGABLE between the two<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||85Josh||04-22-2001||08:37 PM||||Actually, my 85 with the Isuzu 5-speed uses the RED gear, GM part# 10041031. I know this because I lost the old on into the tranny, and went through half of the available gears till this one fit. The speedo and odometer are right on with factory-sized tires.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
